Reciprocity of a random 22x22 resistor mesh: three injection copies
* bench.id: acc_rel_reciprocity_randmesh22
* bench.group: accuracy
* bench.title: Reciprocity v_j(s_k) = v_k(s_j) of a random 22x22 mesh (R log-uniform 1e-2..1e2): 3 copies, 3 relation nodes
* bench.probes: v(r_ab), v(r_ac), v(r_bc), v(an14_13), v(bn5_6), v(an2_17), v(cn5_6), v(bn2_17), v(cn14_13)
* bench.tol.rel: 0
* bench.tol.abs: 1e-9
* bench.expect: match
* bench.oracle: dc_linear
* bench.size: 1457
* bench.tags: linear, op, mesh, relation, twin_block, ill_conditioned, reference_free, reciprocity
* bench.est_rss_mib: 32
* bench.note: Same construction and gate as reciprocity_randmesh14 (K=200, tol.abs 1e-9 = asymmetry <= 5e-12 V), 22x22 mesh, 3 copies, transfer voltages 0.22-0.32 V. The transfer voltages themselves are wrong by only <= 5.1e-11 V (below the default node-voltage tolerance), so only the relation exposes the loss of symmetry. Natural card order (no shuffling needed). Control without the gap: reciprocity_randmesh22_faer.
